<title>GERMANY: Baden Wuerttemberg April CPI up 1.1 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Baden Wuerttemberg April CPI up 1.1 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in the state of Baden-Wuerttemberg were down 0.1 percent in April, with the year-on-year rate rising 1.1 percent, the state's statistics office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In March prices fell 0.2 percent month-on-month and rose 1.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Data for four west German states are used to calculate a preliminary figure for Germany as a whole.  </p>
<p>The Statistics office gave the following breakdown of its April cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.1	+1.1     115.1</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.2	+2.3     125.3</p>
<p> Household energy			  unch	+1.0     100.6</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -3.4	+1.0     119.9</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  -0.2	+0.1     115.3</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods unch	+0.7     112.5</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +0.4	+0.6     110.8</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   unch	+0.3     110.8</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1	+1.2     114.0</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   unch	+2.0     114.8</p>
